# Names only, never values. The tools read the process environment (export these in your shell,
# or run `set -a; . ./.env; set +a` with a private copy of this file named .env, which is git-ignored);
# they do not load this file themselves.
#
# stale-check --live takes the variable NAMES on the command line:
#   --gateway-token-env BIFROST_VIRTUAL_KEY --tavily-key-env TAVILY_API_KEY
# serve-assessment --live reads BIFROST_URL, BIFROST_MODEL, BIFROST_VIRTUAL_KEY and either TAVILY_API_KEY
# or BIFROST_SEARCH_RELAY (the name of a Bifrost relay that holds the Tavily key).
# Real values must never be committed.
# scripts/copilot-check/run.sh passes this GitHub Copilot token only to its temporary local Bifrost container.
GITHUB_COPILOT_API_KEY=
BIFROST_URL=
BIFROST_MODEL=
BIFROST_VIRTUAL_KEY=
TAVILY_API_KEY=
# BIFROST_SEARCH_RELAY=tavily
